Bug 3 — Duplicate rendering of a single element (ghost element)

Description:
A single element is rendered multiple times on the canvas, even though it exists only once.

Observed Behavior:

The same element appears twice on the canvas (see images 3 and 4).

When selecting the “wrong” / additional element:

it can be moved and rotated

but no properties are displayed

When selecting and manipulating the actual (main) element:

the second, incorrect element snaps back to a previous position

Expected Behavior:

Each element should be rendered only once.

Any selectable element should expose its corresponding properties.

Manipulating one element must not affect any non-existent duplicates.